7:41\", \"token_count\": 405, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-50\\n\\n# Slack Thread: CSV Dictionary Loader\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:21] Bob**: Working on the CSV loader for custom dictionary support. I'm thinking we support a simple two-column format: `term,tag`.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:29] Charlie**: Can we support regex in the dictionary too, or is it strictly string matching?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:40] Bob**: For the first pass, I'm just doing exact string matches and case-insensitive substrings. Regex in the dictionary might blow up the processing time if the list gets huge.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 11:41] Alice**: @Bob we need to make sure this works with the existing HIPAA identifiers. If a user adds a custom name to the dictionary, it should be treated with the same priority.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:00] Bob**: Definitely. The `DictionaryMatcher` will run alongside the regex engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:30] Diana**: @Bob what happens if there's a comma in the term? Standard CSV escaping?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 13:32] Bob**: Yeah, I'm using the Python `csv` module with `QUOTE_MINIMAL`. I'll add a test case for quoted terms.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 50 slack thread csv dictionari loader channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 11 21 bob work on the csv loader for custom dictionari support i m think we support a simpl two column format term tag 2026 08 12 11 29 charli can we support regex in the dictionari too or is it strict string match 2026 08 12 11 40 bob for the first pas i m just do exact string match and case insensit substr regex in the dictionari might blow up the process time if the list get huge 2026 08 12 11 41 alic bob we need to make sure this work with the exist hipaa identifi if a user add a custom name to the dictionari it should be treat with the same prioriti 2026 08 12 13 00 bob definit the dictionarymatch will run alongsid the regex engin 2026 08 12 13 30 diana bob what happen if there s a comma in the term standard csv escap 2026 08 12 13 32 bob yeah i m use the python csv modul with quot _ minim i ll add a test case for quot term\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc9244e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"id\": \"d9aa72bd1d956a20\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.331466402126644, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16701060303806295, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7151966, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edc9244e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-csv-dictionary-loader.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1112, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:07\", \"token_count\": 335, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-39\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License Audit\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 11:13] Diana**: Starting the third-party license audit across the dependency tree — need a full inventory before we sign off on anything for release.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:37] Alice**: Watch closely for GPL or AGPL. Our client agreements rule out shipping copyleft code in the core engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:46] Diana**: That's exactly what I'm scanning for, using license-checker against the dependency manifests to flag anything outside MIT/Apache/BSD.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:19] Bob**: Are you following transitive dependencies too? A clean top-level library can still pull in something restrictive underneath.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:24] Diana**: Yes, doing a recursive pass, not just the direct dependencies.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:51] Evan**: Want a hand with the Docker base image layers once the app-level scan is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 14:07] Diana**: That'd help. Still working through the results — nothing conclusive to report yet, I'll have the full inventory soon.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 39 slack thread licens audit channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 09 2026 08 09 11 13 diana start the third parti licens audit across the depend tree need a full inventori befor we sign off on anyth for releas 2026 08 09 12 37 alic watch close for gpl or agpl our client agreement rule out ship copyleft code in the core engin 2026 08 09 12 46 diana that s exact what i m scan for use licens checker against the depend manifest to flag anyth outsid mit apach bsd 2026 08 09 13 19 bob are you follow transit depend too a clean top level librari can still pull in someth restrict underneath 2026 08 09 13 24 diana yes do a recurs pas not just the direct depend 2026 08 09 13 51 evan want a hand with the docker base imag layer onc the app level scan is done 2026 08 09 14 07 diana that d help still work through the result noth conclus to report yet i ll have the full inventori soon\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0111388a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"id\": \"55d2a5f5995c8f55\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.331217442238418, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11960277462631144, \"vector_similarity\": 0.824985, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0111388a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1085, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:15\", \"token_count\": 310, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Original Finding: Ghostscript (AGPLv3)\\n\\nThe initial audit flagged `Ghostscript`, used by the `rasterizer` module for PDF-to-image conversion, as AGPLv3-licensed — on the corporate license blacklist because of its viral copyleft terms for any binary distributed to partner sites.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## First Remediation and Reopen\\n\\nThe team swapped in an alternative PDF parser library to replace the Ghostscript dependency, and that swap was initially marked Completed. On follow-up review, however, the replacement library itself turned out to also be AGPL-licensed — the swap solved the specific Ghostscript dependency but reintroduced the same license category problem one layer down. The task was reopened.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Current Status: Unresolved\\n\\nCharlie is now searching for an Apache 2.0 or MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative that meets the module's rasterization requirements. No suitable replacement has been confirmed yet, so this audit item remains **Active (Reopened)** — not resolved.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Secondary Open Item\\n\\nTesseract OCR itself is Apache 2.0, but the `eng.traineddata` model files were sourced from a community repository and their training-corpus provenance has not been verified as public-domain/CC0. This remains a separate, lower-priority open item pending Evan's trace of the `tessdata_best` provenance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 origin find ghostscript agplv3 the initi audit flag ghostscript use by the raster modul for pdf to imag convers a agplv3 licens on the corpor licens blacklist becaus of it viral copyleft term for ani binari distribut to partner site sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 first remedi and reopen the team swap in an altern pdf parser librari to replac the ghostscript depend and that swap wa initi mark complet on follow up review howev the replac librari itself turn out to also be agpl licens the swap solv the specif ghostscript depend but reintroduc the same licens categori problem one layer down the task wa reopen sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 current status unresolv charli is now search for an apach 20 or mit licens pdf parser altern that meet the modul s raster requir no suitabl replac ha been confirm yet so this audit item remain activ reopen not resolv sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 secondari open item tesseract ocr itself is apach 20 but the eng traineddata model file were sourc from a communiti repositori and their train corpus proven ha not been verifi a public domain cc0 this remain a separ lower prioriti open item pend evan s trace of the tessdata _ best proven\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eec2caee8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"d76c5e15e296ca71\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3275321912646068, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12540620180658116, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7991595, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eec2caee8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1689, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:25\", \"token_count\": 582, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-20\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Local Encryption at Rest — Crypto Evaluation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:02] Bob**: Starting on local encryption at rest. Redacted outputs that hit disk need to be encrypted, and it has to work with no network dependency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:30] Charlie**: Any library lean yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:48] Bob**: Evaluating options for AES-256 that fit the offline runtime. Want something we can ship without cloud KMS.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 13:45] Diana**: Application-level on the outputs, or wrapping the whole volume?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 13:54] Bob**: Application-level on the redacted outputs. More portable across the workstations we're targeting.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 14:03] Alice**: Keep the eval focused on AES-256 at rest for local outputs. Implementation can follow once you've picked a library path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 14:40] Bob**: Will do. Next step after this is wiring the pipeline once the library choice is settled.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 20 slack thread local encrypt at rest crypto evalu channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 03 2026 08 03 11 02 bob start on local encrypt at rest redact output that hit disk need to be encrypt and it ha to work with no network depend 2026 08 03 11 30 charli ani librari lean yet 2026 08 03 11 48 bob evalu option for ae 256 that fit the offlin runtim want someth we can ship without cloud km 2026 08 03 13 45 diana applic level on the output or wrap the whole volum 2026 08 03 13 54 bob applic level on the redact output more portabl across the workstat we re target 2026 08 03 14 03 alic keep the eval focus on ae 256 at rest for local output implement can follow onc you ve pick a librari path 2026 08 03 14 40 bob will do next step after this is wire the pipelin onc the librari choic is settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc587768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/so