d\": \"ee70cc4e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1050, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:34\", \"token_count\": 547, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-21\\n\\n# Slack Thread: AES-256 Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:20] Bob**: Moving forward with the AES-256 pipeline now that the crypto eval settled on it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:28] Bob**: Merged it — every temp file in the processing queue is now encrypted with a per-session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:37] Diana**: Running a stress test. What happens if the system loses power mid-redaction? Does the encrypted temp file persist?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:38] Bob**: Yes, but it's useless without the session key, which only lives in volatile memory. On reboot, the cleanup hook wipes it anyway.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:39] Diana**: Makes sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:23] Diana**: Crypto sign-off done. Verified the `/tmp/cipherdoc` data is unreadable without the session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:41] Diana**: This also builds on the fail-closed work — the pipeline integrates with that deletion behavior cleanly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:43] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:44] Alice**: Nice. :white_check_mark:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 21 slack thread ae 256 encrypt pipelin channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 05 last activ 2026 08 07 2026 08 05 09 20 bob move forward with the ae 256 pipelin now that the crypto eval settl on it 2026 08 05 09 28 bob merg it everi temp file in the process queue is now encrypt with a per session key 2026 08 05 09 37 diana run a stress test what happen if the system lose power mid redact doe the encrypt temp file persist 2026 08 05 09 38 bob yes but it s useless without the session key which onli life in volatil memori on reboot the cleanup hook wipe it anyway 2026 08 05 09 39 diana make sens 2026 08 07 13 23 diana crypto sign off done verifi the tmp cipherdoc data is unread without the session key 2026 08 07 13 41 diana this also build on the fail close work the pipelin integr with that delet behavior clean 2026 08 07 13 43 bob call this done 2026 08 07 13 44 alic nice white _ check _ mark\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edd058fe8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"id\": \"e93358efaffe30a1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3377451094524277, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.146387756360611, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7842456, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edd058fe8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1112, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:01\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-30\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Worker Pool Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:09] Charlie**: Sketching out a worker pool model for local batch processing. It has to slot into the existing batch CLI rather than replace it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:41] Bob**: Threads or separate processes? Given how CPU-heavy the redaction pass is, threads alone probably won't buy us much.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:43] Charlie**: Leaning toward processes for that reason. Still working out how workers get handed files without duplicating too much per-worker state.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:19] Alice**: Does this need to wait on anything, or can it move independently of the CLI work?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:36] Charlie**: It builds on top of the completed CLI, so the interface has to stay compatible, but the pool itself can be developed on its own.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:37] Diana**: One thing to keep in mind — if files are processed out of order across workers, the audit log ordering needs to still make sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 12:44] Charlie**: Good catch, I'll fold that into the design before I start wiring it up.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 30 slack thread batch worker pool design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 03 2026 08 03 11 09 charli sketch out a worker pool model for local batch process it ha to slot into the exist batch cli rather than replac it 2026 08 03 11 41 bob thread or separ process given how cpu heavi the redact pas is thread alon probabl won t buy u much 2026 08 03 11 43 charli lean toward process for that reason still work out how worker get hand file without duplic too much per worker state 2026 08 03 12 19 alic doe this need to wait on anyth or can it move independ of the cli work 2026 08 03 12 36 charli it build on top of the complet cli so the interfac ha to stay compat but the pool itself can be develop on it own 2026 08 03 12 37 diana one thing to keep in mind if file are process out of order across worker the audit log order need to still make sens 2026 08 03 12 44 charli good catch i ll fold that into the design befor i start wire it up\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede60b2c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"id\": \"76069273edbb9de1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3237592174524277, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.146387756360611, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73762596, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede60b2c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-batch-worker-pool-design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1139, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:43\", \"token_count\": 331, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee16ca328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"4951fb04269a3c9b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32288369397823524, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13724508425462187, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75604045, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee16ca328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:57\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-48\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Hotspots\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-17\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:16] Bob**: Running into some weirdness with memory. The long-running container is hitting the memory limit after about 4 hours of processing. Looks like a slow leak.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:34] Charlie**: Is it in the engine or the API layer? If we're not clearing the regex caches, that could be it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:37] Bob**: I'm seeing the RSS climb even when the API is idle after a batch. I suspect something in the `DocumentProcessor` isn't closing file handles or clearing buffers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:38] Charlie**: Ugh.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:50] Diana**: I can confirm this on the staging node. I've been watching the Grafana dashboard and it's a steady 45-degree angle upward. No dips.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:15] Evan**: I've bumped the limit to 2GB temporarily so we don't keep crashing, but we need a real fix. @Bob are you using `tracemalloc` yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:16] Bob**: Just starting a run with it now. I'll dump the snapshots and see where the allocations are sticking.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:17] Alice**: @Bob if this is a deep issue in the engine core, we might need to pull Charlie in full-time on this.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:18] Charlie**: Already looking at the `pdfminer` wrappers. We've had issues with its object recycling before.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 48 slack thread memori leak hotspot channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 17 2026 08 17 10 16 bob run into some weird with memori the long run contain is hit the memori limit after about 4 hour of process look like a slow leak 2026 08 17 10 34 charli is it in the engin or the api layer if we re not clear the regex cach that could be it 2026 08 17 10 37 bob i m see the rss climb even when the api is idl after a batch i suspect someth in the documentprocessor isn t close file handl or clear buffer 2026 08 17 10 38 charli ugh 2026 08 17 10 50 diana i can confirm this on the stage node i ve been watch the grafana dashboard and it s a steadi 45 degre angl upward no dip 2026 08 17 11 15 evan i ve bump the limit to 2gb temporarili so we don t keep crash but we need a real fix bob are you use tracemalloc yet 2026 08 17 11 16 bob just start a run with it now i ll dump the snapshot and see where the alloc are stick 2026 08 17 11 17 alic bob if this is a deep issu in the engin core we might need to pull charli in full time on this 2026 08 17 11 18 charli alreadi look at the pdfminer wrapper we ve had issu with it object recycl befor\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edeb07bc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"id\": \"f8eeaf3fd344f2f9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.322067854337039, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12056697619576998, \"vector_similarity\": 0.79223657, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edeb07bc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-memory-leak-hotspots.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1370, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:36\", \"token_count\": 421, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-44\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Merge\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:19] Charlie**: Merged the stream-chunking implementation into mainline. Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:21] Alice**: Great, this was overdue. Nice work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:57] Bob**: Anything left over from the memory concerns during testing, or is it fully clean?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 10:00] Charlie**: As far as testing showed, clean. We'll see if anything shows up on longer runs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:01] Charlie**: Following up on the leak Bob found on the larger files — root cause was the chunk buffers not being explicitly released once a worker moved past them. Refactoring the buffer-release path now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:15] Bob**: Does the fix release eagerly after each chunk, or wait until the whole file finishes?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:18] Charlie**: Eagerly, right after each chunk is processed — that's the whole point, don't let it accumulate. Still working through it, not ready to call it done again yet.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:51] Diana**: Let me know when there's a build to re-run the stress case against.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 44 slack thread larg file chunk merg channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 16 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 08 16 09 19 charli merg the stream chunk implement into mainlin call this done 2026 08 16 09 21 alic great this wa overdu nice work 2026 08 16 09 57 bob anyth left over from the memori concern dure test or is it fulli clean 2026 08 16 1000 charli a far a test show clean we ll see if anyth show up on longer run 2026 08 20 09 01 charli follow up on the leak bob found on the larger file root caus wa the chunk buffer not be explicit releas onc a worker move past them refactor the buffer releas path now 2026 08 20 09 15 bob doe the fix releas eager after each chunk or wait until the whole file finish 2026 08 20 09 18 charli eager right after each chunk is process that s the whole point don t let it accumul still work through it not readi to call it done again yet 2026 08 20 09 51 diana let me know when there s a build to re run the stress case against\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eddd6ab28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"id\": \"05a1fa41d5d18ab3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32012184983602715, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09796066833718167, \"vector_similarity\": 0.83849794, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eddd6ab